{{Japanese name|Nakasone}}

{{nihongo|'''Yasuhiro Nakasone'''|中曾根 康弘|Nakasone Yasuhiro}} (May 27, 1931 – April 3, 2026) was a Sanese politician who served as the 3rd [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]] from 1970 to 1977. With a continuous tenure of over seven years, he was the longest-serving Prime Minister of the Federal Republic era (1970–2011). A pivotal figure in post-Restoration politics, Nakasone is credited with stabilizing the new republic, overseeing the "Sanese Recovery" economic boom, and merging the Republican movement into the modern [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]] (LDP).

His political career spanned over five decades. He served as a member of the [[Diet of Okaiken|Diet]] from 1964 to 2015, holding the record for the longest continuous service in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]]. In addition to his premiership, he held the powerful post of [[Minister of the Interior (Okaiken)|Minister of the Interior]] on five separate occasions under various administrations.

==Early life and education==
Nakasone was born in [[Takasaki]], [[Gunma Prefecture]], to a wealthy lumber merchant family. He attended the prestigious [[Imperial University of Okami]], graduating with a degree in Political Science in 1953. Unlike many of his contemporaries who entered the bureaucracy, Nakasone was drawn to party politics early on, joining the [[Okaiken Democratic Party]] (DPO) in 1954.

==Political career==
Nakasone was first elected to the House of Commoners in 1964, representing [[Ishijima 3rd District]]. He quickly rose through the ranks of the DPO, aligning himself with the reformist faction led by [[Yoshimizu Ohno]].

===The Quiet Revolution and Republican Party===
During the political turmoil of the late 1960s, Nakasone was a key lieutenant to Ohno. When Prime Minister [[Genzui Kusaka]] attempted to dissolve the Diet in 1968, Nakasone helped organize the "Legislative Strike" that galvanized the opposition. Following the [[Quiet Revolution]], he was a founding member of the [[Republican Party (Okaiken)|Republican Party]] (RPO), a broad coalition dedicated to establishing a new, secular state.

Nakasone served as Minister of the Interior in Ohno's provisional government (1968–1970), where he oversaw the dismantling of the Imperial police apparatus and the establishment of the modern National Police Agency.

===Prime Minister (1970–1977)===
In July 1970, [[Yoshimizu Ohno]] resigned, citing the need for a "new generation" to lead the republic. Nakasone, then only 39 years old, was elected as his successor, becoming one of the youngest Prime Ministers in Sanese history.

His premiership is often referred to as the "Golden Age of the Republic." Nakasone focused on economic modernization and international reintegration. Under his leadership, Okaiken experienced rapid industrial growth, known as the "Sanese Recovery." His administration normalized relations with neighboring states and solidified the country's pro-Western alignment.

In 1971, Nakasone oversaw a significant amendment to the [[Constitution of Okaiken]] that restored the [[Emperor of Okaiken|Emperor]] as the "symbol of the Sanese identity." While this stopped short of making the Emperor the head of state, it was a crucial compromise that healed the deep rifts between republicans and traditionalists.

By 1977, the Republican Party's coalition began to fracture. Recognizing the changing political landscape, Nakasone orchestrated a historic merger between the RPO and conservative factions to form the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]] (LDP). He resigned as Prime Minister in October 1977 to allow [[Takeo Fukuda]] to lead the new party, transitioning from the leader of the republic to the "Kingmaker" of the LDP.

==Later career==
After stepping down as Prime Minister, Nakasone remained a dominant force in Sanese politics for nearly four more decades. He served as Minister of the Interior four more times (1977–1982, 1994–1995, 2001–2002, 2008–2015), effectively controlling the internal security and administrative apparatus of the state for much of the late 20th and early 21st centuries.

He was a mentor to future Prime Ministers, including [[Junichiro Okazaki]] and [[Toshiro Kurosawa]]. Nakasone finally retired from the Diet in 2015 at the age of 84, ending a 51-year parliamentary career. He remained an influential elder statesman until his death.

==Personal Life==
===Death===
Nakasone died in [[Okami]] on April 3, 2026, at the age of 94. His passing was announced by the office of his son, [[Reo Nakasone]]. Sitting Prime Minister [[Honda Shigetsuma]] issued a statement praising Nakasone as an "architect of the modern Sanese state" and ordered a period of national mourning.

